A||||2||Shaun41178||Computer controlling A/F ratio @ WOT???||||1
Z||000000||Shaun41178||10-17-1999||10:12 PM||||I have a opportunity to buy 19# injectors for a really great price.  These injectors have only 3000k miles on them and cost $450 new and are the Tomco injectors sold by Summit and other speed shops and such.  I plan on using these injectors in my 3.2 rebuild that I also plan on running nitrous through.  I expect to have around 300 hp and don't expect the stock injectors to be able to keep up.<P>My question is, does the computer control the air/fuel ratio at Wide Open Throttle?  If so, is there a program in the computer that tells  that it should try to keep the air/fuel ratio at a certain parameter?  Like with the stock engine and fuel system, when the car goes WOT does the computer dump as much fuel in as possible to keep from running lean or does it try to keep it at a constant a/f ratio for maximum performance?  Maximum performance is achieved with about a 12.5:1-13-1 air/fuel ratio.  Does anyone know what I am talking about here?<P>Like with 19# injectors I don't want too much fuel being dumped into the engine hurting performance.  For example with my 3.2 if I don't run nitrous I don't want an excessive amount of fuel being dumped into the cylinders making my a/f ratio like 11:1 killing power cause it is too rich.<P>This is why I am asking if the computer trys to maintain a certain air/fuel ratio under WOT to obtain maximum performance.  So does it?  <P>SOMEONE MUST KNOW!!!!!!! ||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||10-17-1999||10:31 PM||||A couple of answers here...<P>First, no, the O2 is never in control of the fuel at WOT. There are basically two methods:<BR>1. Lock the BLM and INT to 128 and add fuel per the power enrichment tables.<BR>2. Use the last BLM and INT values and add fuel per the power enrichment tables.<P>Depending on the application, there is either one AFR for WOT or a table of enrichments vs RPM and temp.<P>One reason I switched to another ECM. The Fiero V6 (6869/7170) are good, but lack some of the fining tuning for AE and PE.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pretender||10-18-1999||02:12 AM||||have you thought about running a air-fuel controller like the super afc?(made by Apec) An EGT gauge would also help you tune your system. My friend runs these in his talon and they have made the difference for him(running low 12's). L8r.||||reg||10
